                        <div
                            class="bg-purple-500/10 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-400 px-3 py-1 rounded text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-purple-500/20">
                            Complex Integration
                        </div>
                        <i class="fas fa-sync-alt text-brand-muted text-2xl group-hover:text-brand-accent transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-text mb-3">Sports League Bi-Directional Sync</h2>

                    <p class="text-brand-muted mb-6 leading-relaxed flex-grow">
                        <strong>The Challenge:</strong> Onboarding a multi-tenant Sports League (10+ clubs) with a
                        volatile ecosystem. They required a bi-directional sync between B2B CRMs, mobile apps, and
                        gamification platforms. We had to handle conflicting data edits and push segmented audiences
                        back to their CRM.
                        <br><br>
                        <strong>My Solution:</strong> Architected the logic flow for a 2-way sync to resolve data
                        conflicts (Source of Truth logic). I coordinated the integration across Ticketing, E-commerce,
                        and Membership systems to ensure data consistency.
                        <br><br>
                        <strong>The Outcome:</strong> Established a closed-loop data ecosystem, allowing clubs to
                        push highly targeted segments from our platform back to their CRM for sales execution.
                    </p>

                    <div class="border-t border-brand-muted/10 pt-4 mt-auto">
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                            <span
                                class="text-xs font-mono text-brand-muted bg-brand-bg px-2 py-1 rounded">Bi-Directional
                                Sync</span>
                            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-brand-muted bg-brand-bg px-2 py-1 rounded">CRM
                                Architecture</span>
                            <span
                                class="text-xs font-mono text-brand-muted bg-brand-bg px-2 py-1 rounded">Multi-Tenant</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div
                class="group bg-brand-surface rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-brand-muted/10 hover:shadow-glow hover:border-brand-accent/30 transition-all duration-300">
                <div class="p-8 h-full flex flex-col">
                    <div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-4">
                        <div
                            class="bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-400 px-3 py-1 rounded text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-emerald-500/20">
                            Enterprise Governance
                        </div>
                        <i class="fas fa-shield-alt text-brand-muted text-2xl group-hover:text-brand-accent transition-colors" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-text mb-3">Fortune 500 Data Lake Strategy</h2>

                    <p class="text-brand-muted mb-6 leading-relaxed flex-grow">
                        <strong>The Challenge:</strong> A Fortune 500 client with rigid Data Lake pipelines needed to
                        onboard massive "Non-Adult" membership datasets. Privacy compliance was critical: we needed to
                        target parents/guardians without exposing minor's PII, involving strict legal constraints.
                        <br><br>
                        <strong>My Solution:</strong> Led the technical discovery with their Data Engineers. I designed
                        a "Parent/Guardian" entity model that routed all communications to authorized adults while
                        keeping the non-adult profile data strictly siloed for analysis only.
                        <br><br>
                        <strong>The Outcome:</strong> The model was signed off by the client's own data-protection and
                        engineering teams and shipped, letting them reach the guardian audience without minors' personal
                        data leaving the analytics silo.
                    </p>

                    <div class="border-t border-brand-muted/10 pt-4 mt-auto">
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                            <span
                                class="text-xs font-mono text-brand-muted bg-brand-bg px-2 py-1 rounded">Privacy/GDPR</span>
                            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-brand-muted bg-brand-bg px-2 py-1 rounded">Data
                                Modeling</span>
                            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-brand-muted bg-brand-bg px-2 py-1 rounded">ETL
                                Strategy</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
